# Excludes from the Docker build context shipped to the daemon.
# Anything matched here is NOT visible inside the build, regardless of
# whether the Dockerfile would have COPY'd it. Trimming the context keeps
# the per-build upload small and stops a stray .env from accidentally
# landing in an image layer.
#
# Build context: `projects/atrium/` (NOT the repo root). The Dockerfile
# re-installs and re-builds inside the image, so every install artifact
# below is rebuilt and must be excluded so a stale host `.next` /
# `node_modules` never shadows the in-image build.
#
# WINDOWS-EPERM CONTEXT: the Windows host's `.next/standalone` is emitted
# with EPERM symlink warnings (no admin / Developer Mode). By excluding
# `**/.next` here, the host's broken standalone trace can never leak into
# the image — the Linux build stage produces a clean standalone from
# scratch (where symlink tracing works). The apex/razors-edge precedent.

# Workspace install + build artifacts — rebuilt inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/.cache
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache
**/playwright/.cache

# Local environment files — secrets. atrium needs NO runtime secrets
# (web-only, static index — ADR-001); the only config is the build-time
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` ARG, set in the Dockerfile, not from a
# checked-in env file.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Logs.
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Test + review surfaces — never executed at runtime. The whole `e2e/`
# tree (Playwright, the README screenshot harness, its own node_modules)
# and the unit tests live here.
**/__tests__
**/__fixtures__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
e2e
**/playwright.config.ts
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.lighthouseci
lighthouserc.json
web/lighthouserc.json

# Per-project docs — readable on GitHub, not needed in the runtime image.
**/README.md
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/PLAN.md
**/PROGRESS.md
**/DECISIONS.md
**/AGENT_NOTES.md
**/CRITIQUE-*.md
**/REVIEW-*.md
**/DEPLOY.md
docs

# The build / deploy descriptors themselves — they tell the build what to
# do; they do not belong inside the resulting image.
fly.toml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Git metadata — not needed at runtime, and a stray fragment of the
# repo's history in a layer is a leak surface.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
